1947-04-26|Barrier Miner (Broken Hill) · Family Notices, Engagement|2|Zubrinich|Irene Dawn Zubrinich, married McAvaney|«ZUBRINICH — McAVANEY — the engagement is announced of Irene Dawn, youngest daughter of Mr. and Mrs. L. J. Zubrinich, of 178 Murton Street, to Edward John (Jack), only son of Mr. and Mrs. Herb McAvaney» — the third daughter, not in the tree|48495417
1949-07-22|Barrier Miner (Broken Hill) · Family Notices, Birth|7|Zubrinich|John Rex McAvaney, grandson|«McAVANEY (née Zubrinich) — A son was born to Mr. and Mrs. Jack McAvaney … The names chosen for the new arrival are John Rex. Mrs. McAvaney was formerly Miss Dawn Zubrinich» — a grandson confirming the 1948 marriage held|48609250
1917-03-08|Barrier Miner (Broken Hill) · Family Notices, In Memoriam|2|Zubrinich|Kate and Jack Zubrinich, possible lead|«Inserted by his loving wife and children, Alice Murphy, KATE AND JACK ZUBRINICH, Mary and Joe Russ, Dock and Barney Murphy» — mourning Stephen Murphy. A KATE married a JACK ZUBRINICH, daughter of Stephen and Alice Murphy of Broken Hill. NOT YET RECONCILED with John William Zubrinich (1885-1953), whose tree spouse is «Catherine Lucy Murphy» — Kate is an ordinary short form of Catherine, and «Jack» of John. Not asserted as the same couple; flagged for the next sweep|45396740
1930-12-17|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Death|2|Zubrinich|John Zubrinich, husband of Rose|«ZUBRINICH — On December 15, 1930, at his residence, 13 Three Chain Road, Solomontown, John, dearly beloved husband of Rose Zubrinich, AGED 72 YEARS». THE DAY IS THE TREE'S 15 DECEMBER 1930 AND THE PLACE IS PORT PIRIE; THE AGE IS NOT — born 6 March 1860 he would be 70, so the notice puts his birth two years earlier|95813556
1931-01-01|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Thanks|2|Zubrinich|The widow, sons and daughters of the late John Zubrinich|«The widow, sons, and daughters of the late John Zubrinich wish to sincerely THANK all kind friends» — a widow, more than one son and more than one daughter survive him|95969115
1933-12-16|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, In Memoriam|2|Zubrinich|His wife, a son and daughters|«In loving memory of our dear husband and father, who passed away on December 15, 1930 … Inserted by his loving wife, son, and daughters, Krug [sic, as OCR], Florrie, and Phyllis» — the date, three years on|96090706
1936-09-02|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Approaching marriage|2|Zubrinich|Phyllis C. Zubrinich, married Burt|«ZUBRINICH-BURT — The marriage of Phyllis C., youngest daughter of Mrs. and the late Mr. J. Zubrinich, of Solomontown, to Reginald H., youngest son of Mr. and Mrs. B. Burt» at St. Anthony's Hall, Solomontown, on 7 September 1936. The father is already dead, which fits John of 1930|95892533
