1937-10-09|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Approaching marriage|2|Zubrinich|Vida Zubrinich, married Smith|«ZUBRINICH — SMITH — The marriage of Vida, second daughter of Mr. and Mrs. T. L. Zubrinich, of Solomontown, to Allan, younger son of Mr. and Mrs. W. Smith» at Central Methodist Church, Port Pirie, on 19 October 1937|96124375
1938-08-05|The Transcontinental (Port Augusta) · Family Notices, Wedding|3|Zubrinich|Keith Leo Zubrinich, married Rowe|«ZUBRINICH—ROWE — At Port Augusta Methodist Church, Saturday, July 23. Keith, eldest son of Mr. and Mrs. T. L. Zubrinich, of Solomontown, and Rita, youngest daughter of Mrs. V. and the late Mr. W. Rowe» — the wedding of 23 July 1938|168222252
1918-11-09|Port Pirie Recorder · Family Notices, Birth|2|Zubrinich|Gwenneth Florence, daughter of A. L. Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH — On the 24th October [1918], at Mrs Duffy's Nursing Home, Pirie West, to Mr and Mrs A. L. Zubrinich — a daughter, Gwenneth Florence»|95424284
1921-12-10|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Birth|2|Zubrinich|A son of A. L. Zubrinich, first named James Bernard|«ZUBRINICH — On 1st December, at Nurse Duffy's Home, 20 Goode road, Pirie West, to Mr and Mrs A. L. Zubrinich, a son — JAMES BERNARD»|95383211
1921-12-12|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Birth|2|Zubrinich|The same son, now named Leslie Bernard|«… to Mr. and Mrs. A. L. Zubrinich, a son — LESLIE BERNARD» — the same couple, the same home and the same day, with a different first name two days later. A CORRECTION, NOT TWO CHILDREN; the child's own registration would say which|95383293
1924-08-09|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Birth|2|Zubrinich|Terrence Joseph, son of Jack Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH — At their residence, Solomontown, to Mr. and Mrs. Jack Zubrinich — a son. (Terrence Joseph.)» The tree has him born 5 August 1924 at Solomontown; the notice is of Saturday the 9th, so it agrees|96104089
1940-04-09|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Death|2|Zubrinich|Arthur Clive Zubrinich, aged 7|«ZUBRINICH — On April 8, 1940, at Port Pirie Hospital, ARTHUR CLIVE, beloved SON of Mr. and Mrs. M. J. Zubrinich, of 56 Simpson road, Pirie South, aged 7 years»; the next day's notice adds «brother of June, Claire, Noel and Ivan». A son of Maurice Joseph Zubrinich (1900-1973), not in the tree|96329636
1949-09-26|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Death|2|Zubrinich|Rose Zubrinich, widow of John|«ZUBRINICH — On September 24 at Port Pirie Hospital, ROSE, relict of John Zubrinich, of 13 Three Chain road, Solomontown. Aged 89» — the widow of the John who died there on 15 December 1930. The address is the same house. She is in no tree; aged 89 puts her birth about 1860|96219660
1953-12-18|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Death|6|Zubrinich|John William Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH — On December 17 at his residence, 143 Main road, Solomontown, John William, beloved husband of Catherine Zubrinich, loving father of Jack, Len, Morrie, and Terence. Aged 68». THE TREE HAS 16 DECEMBER 1953; the notice says the 17th, and the later in-memoriam says the 19th. Aged 68 agrees with a birth of 5 March 1885. A father of Morrie (Maurice, b. 1922) and Terence (b. 1924), both in the tree|96230482
1955-12-23|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, In Memoriam|12|Zubrinich|Jack, by his daughters|«In loving memory of our dear father, Jack, who passed away on December 19, 1953. Always remembered by Carrie, Dot, and family» — a third date for the same death, from his daughters two years on|296331793
1948-07-30|The Whyalla News · Family Notices, Death|1|Zubrinich|John Zubrinich, aged 14|«ZUBRINICH — On July 29, at Prince Alfred Hospital, Melbourne, Victoria, John, dearly beloved son of Jack and Rene Zubrinich and loving brother of [two siblings, not named here: they may be living]. Aged 14 years»; the Adelaide Advertiser of 5 August gives him as «John Frederick, eldest son of Mr. and Mrs. J. S. Zubrinich, of Whyalla». A son of John Stephen Zubrinich (1907-1999), in the tree, and not himself in it|196823445
1940-05-15|The Advertiser (Adelaide) · Family Notices, Marriage|12|Zubrinich|Phyllis B. Zubrinich to Cecil V. White, Port Pirie|«ZUBRINICH—WHITE.—The marriage of Phyllis B., third daughter of Mr. and Mrs. T. L. Zubrinich, of Solomontown, to Cecil V., only son of Mr. and Mrs. G. White, of Port Pirie, will be solemnised in the cetral Methodist Church, Port Pirie, on Saturday, the 18th of …» — the notice is of Wednesday the 15th, so Saturday the 18th is 18 May 1940. T. L. matches Thomas Leo Zubrinich (b. 9 July 1892) in the tree by initials only; his children are not in the tree|47192418
1940-07-19|The Advertiser (Adelaide) · Family Notices, Engagement|10|Zubrinich|Gwenyth Florence Zubrinich to Andrew Keith McKnight|«ZUBRINICH — McKNIGHT.—The engagement is announced of Gwenyth Florence, only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. A. L. Zubrinich of Solomontown, to Andrew Keith, elder son of Mr. and Mrs. A. S. McKnight, of Port Augusta.» A. L. matches Arthur Leslie Zubrinich (b. 10 Dec 1897) in the tree by initials; the same notice ran in The Chronicle of 25 July (id 92392576)|47204560
1941-11-28|The Transcontinental (Port Augusta) · Family Notices, Wedding report|1|Zubrinich|Zubrinich–McKnight wedding at Port Pirie|«Zubrinich Wedding … The … Catholic Presbytery was the scene on Saturday evening last of the marriage of Andrew Keith, elder son of Mr. and Mrs. A. S. McKnight, of Port Augusta, to Gweneth Florence, only daughter of Mr. and …» — the Saturday before the 28th is 22 November 1941; the OCR reads «Pine» for Pirie. The engagement of July 1940 came to a wedding seventeen months later|168452455
1942-01-29|The Advertiser (Adelaide) · Family Notices, Engagement|10|Zubrinich|Edna May Furze to Malcolm Theodore Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH.—The engagement is announced of Edna May, second daughter of Mr. and Mrs. H. P. Furze, of Solomontown, to Malcolm Theodore, eldest son of Mr. and Mrs E. M. Zubrinich, of Solomontown.» E. M. matches Edward Malcolm Zubrinich (b. 29 Apr 1895) in the tree by initials; his children are not in the tree|45749498
1943-01-04|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Engagement|2|Zubrinich|Patricia Dunning to Maurice Zubrinich, third son of J. Zubrinich of Main road|«ZUBRINICH.—The engagement is announced of Patricia, second daughter of Mr. and Mrs. J. Dunning, of 36 Eighth street, Pirie West, and Maurice, third son of Mr. and Mrs. J. Zubrinich, of Main road, Solomontown.» THE PARENTS ARE JOHN WILLIAM (1885-1953) AND KATE: his death notice of December 1953 gives his address as 143 Main road, Solomontown, and names a son Morrie. The tree has Maurice William (b. 7 Mar 1922) as his son, the third of the four sons the 1953 notice names|96354521
1943-05-14|The Advertiser (Adelaide) · Family Notices, Engagement|8|Zubrinich|Joy Zubrinich to Peter Charles Leuders, Renmark|«ZUBRINICH — LEUDERS. —The engagement is announced of Joy, only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. E. M. Zubrinich, of Port Pirie, to Peter Charles, only son of Mr. and Mrs. J. A. Leuders, of Renmark.» The same E. M. as the engagement of Edna May's husband, so Joy is Malcolm Theodore's sister; the Chronicle repeats it on 20 May (id 92369960)|48912599
1943-11-01|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Engagement|2|Zubrinich|Mollie Dorraine Manser to Kevin Edward Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH.—The engagement is announced of Mollie Dorraine, only child of the late Mr. G. Manser, of Port Pirie, to Kevin Edward, second son of Mr. and Mrs. T. L. Zubrinich, of Solomontown.» Kevin is a brother of Phyllis B. (1940), the same T. L.|96200878
1944-06-21|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Marriage|3|Zubrinich|Edna May Furze to Malcolm Theodore Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH.-The marriage of Edna May, second daughter of Mr. and Mrs. H. P. Furze, Solomontown, to Malcolm Theodore (A.I.F., ret. N.G.), eldest son of Mr. and Mrs. E. M. Zubrinich, Solomontown, will be solemnised at the Solomontown Methodist Church on Saturday …» The Adelaide Advertiser of 22 June (id 43209417) gives Saturday 24 June 1944, 7 p.m. The engagement of January 1942 came to a wedding thirty months later, with the groom home from New Guinea|96266287
1944-08-09|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Marriage|3|Zubrinich|Kathleen Mary Flinn to Leslie Bernard Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH—FLINN.—The marriage of Kathleen Mary, elder daughter of Mr. and Mrs. F. J. Flinn, of Pirie West, to Leslie Bernard (R.A.N., ret.), eldest son of Mr. and Mrs. A. L. Zubrinich, of Solomontown, will be solemnised at St. Mark's Church with Nuptial Mass o…» (the day is cut off in the OCR). LESLIE BERNARD IS THE BABY OF DECEMBER 1921: the Recorder birth notice of 1 December 1921 gives a son to Mr and Mrs A. L. Zubrinich, first named James Bernard, and on the 12th corrects it to Leslie Bernard. The same A. L., so Gwenyth Florence (1940) is his sister|96168817
1945-02-16|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Engagement|2|Zubrinich|Betty Patricia Zubrinich to Rollo Teague, Jamestown|«… Zubrinich, of Solomontown, announce the engagement of their youngest daughter, Betty Patricia, to Rollo (R.A.A.F.), only son of Mr. and Mrs. M. V. Teague, of Jamestown.» The Advertiser of 19 February (id 43481319) gives the parents as Mr. and Mrs. T. L. Zubrinich, so she is the sister of Phyllis B. and Kevin Edward|96193625
1945-09-28|The Advertiser (Adelaide) · Family Notices, Marriage|16|Zubrinich|Rose Joy Zubrinich to Peter Charles Leuders|«… Zubrinich, 65 Queen street, Solomontown, to Peter Charles, only son of Mr and Mrs T A. Leuders, 163 Fifteenth street, Renmark. At Solomontown Methodist Church, on Saturday, September 29, at 6 p.m. Reception in Parish Hall.» The Murray Pioneer of Renmark the day before (id 109413786) names her Rose Joy. The 1943 engagement came to a wedding thirty months later; Joy's parents are Mr. and Mrs. E. M. Zubrinich|48669699
1945-11-15|The Advertiser (Adelaide) · Family Notices, Marriage|12|Zubrinich|Mollie Dorraine Manser to Kevin Edward Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH.—The marriage of Mollie Dorraine, granddaughter of Mrs. B. Manser, of Whyalla, to Kevin Edward, second son of Mr. and Mrs. T. L. Zubrinich, of Solomontown, will be solemnised at Central Baptist Church, Port Pirie, on Saturday, November 17, at 7 p.m.» An announcement beforehand, not a report; the 17th of November 1945 was a Saturday|48677522
1946-05-23|The Advertiser (Adelaide) · Family Notices, Engagement|14|Zubrinich|Edith Claire Zubrinich to Rex Glynde Sandercock, Keswick|«ZUBRINICH — SANDERCOCK. — The engagement is anounced of Edith Claire, second daughter of Mr. and Mrs. M. J. Zubrinich, Simpson St., Port Pirie, to Rex Glynde, only son of Mr. and Mrs. A. M. Sandercock, Keswick, Adelaide.» M. J. is Maurice Joseph Zubrinich (b. 1900), whose son Arthur Clive died at 56 Simpson road in April 1940, the same house; Edith Claire is the Claire named among the brothers and sisters in that notice|35695969
1946-07-24|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Marriage|3|Zubrinich|Edith Claire Zubrinich to Rex Glynde Sandercock|«ZUBRINICH — SANDERCOCK.—The marriage of Edith Claire, second daughter of Mr. and Mrs. M. J. Zubrinich, of 56 Simpson road, Solomontown, to Rex Glynde, only son of Mr. and Mrs. A. M. Sandercock, of Keswick, will be solemnised at Solomontown Methodist Church …» The Advertiser of 26 July (id 35706514) gives Saturday 27 July 1946, 6.30 p.m. Engagement to wedding, two months|96158721
1946-11-13|The Recorder (Port Pirie) · Family Notices, Engagement|3|Zubrinich|Joanna Marion Josephine Clowes to Stanley Joseph Zubrinich|«ZUBRINICH.—The engagement is announced of Joanna Marion Josephine, only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. W. G. Clowes, of Margate, Queensland, to Stanley Joseph, second son of Mr. and Mrs. A. L. Zubrinich, of Solomontown.» A third child of A. L., after Leslie Bernard and Gwenyth Florence|96162517
